# Test: O2 (triplet ground state) PUMP2 / cc-pVDZ
# Open-shell triplet (9 alpha / 7 beta electrons).
#
# Reference (Gaussian g09, frozen_core=auto):
#   UMP2  energy : -149.9731825 Ha
#   <S^2> (UMP2) :   2.0343
#   PUMP2 energy : -149.9789090 Ha
#   <S^2>_A      :   2.0006
#   PUMP2 correction = -5.7265 mHa
#
# CAUTION: O2 is moderately spin-contaminated (Delta<S^2> = 0.0331 for the
# triplet state); the cross-doubles-only formula overshoots in magnitude
# vs g09 PMP2-0 by ~1.5 mHa.  See PUMP2_FORMULA.md for the source of the
# residual (singles + same-spin doubles couplings, not yet implemented).
#
# StudDFT v0.63.x output (cross-doubles only):
#   PUMP2 correction = -7.2340 mHa     (residual: -1.51e-3 Ha vs g09)
#
%method  MP2
%basis   cc-pVDZ
%spherical
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    3
! v1.25.6: the guess is PINNED.  This input historically ran with the
! default guess, whose meaning drifted from CORE to SAD around v1.20;
! the SAD guess puts O2 on a ridge between UHF solutions and the
! basin choice becomes toolchain arithmetic: the container (gfortran
! 13, reference BLAS) rolls into a METASTABLE solution 0.166 Ha above
! the true UHF minimum, while a gfortran-11 + OpenBLAS cluster rolls
! into the true one -- and a historical mass re-record silently
! swallowed the container's flip, corrupting the anchor to the wrong
! basin (see BENCHMARK_NOTES_v1.25.6.md).  CORE converges to the true
! solution (UHF -149.6277, <S**2> = 2.033, matching the g09 header
! values above) on both toolchains tested.
%initial_guess core
%spin    unrestricted
%pump2   yes
%frozen_core 2

*geometry angstrom
O   0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
O   0.000000   0.000000   1.207690
*end
